    {
      "id": "decl-boundary",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
        "body": "- Declaration does not render content. Rendering the graph's actual material is View and Content's job; Declaration only names which node fills each presentation role.\n- Declaration does not own node positions or layout. Where nodes sit on the canvas is unrelated to identity.\n- Declaration does not define *how* an exposed view looks — only *which* node is assigned to that role.\n- Declaration does not grant runtime capability beyond what `authority` explicitly states. Absence of a grant means the action is not permitted, not that it's merely undocumented.\n- Declaration is not a template. It describes one graph's own identity, not a reusable composition pattern for building other graphs (see Templates).\n- Declaration does not vouch for which custom node types are safe to use in the graph. That authority comes from Bridges, one per type, each pointing at a real class definition.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
