    {
      "id": "decl-examples",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Examples",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 440
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Examples",
        "body": "**Examples live outside the primitive, referenced, not embedded.**\n\n**Weekend Reading Group** is a small plan graph whose Declaration is a Custom Declaration: bound to the Custom Declaration class, allowed to use it by an import bridge, drawn as a card that shows its own name, kind and version, and edited with the complete form. It has one Surface (a plan, a summary, an icon, then a glyph) and a landing page, and it is laid out the way the Declaration Template teaches. Open it with the portal beside this node.\n\nThe Declaration Template itself is the other reference: a page that explains each part of a Declaration and walks through building one.\n\nNo canon graph has a Custom Declaration yet; the example linked here is still in a personal library.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "definitionKey": "page-section",
